!
! How many freights a file of size bytes takes at k data rows a freight,
! in Trebago (pollen_rules.h PR1): zxvd's freight.pack carries 20 bytes a
! data row, so ceil(size / (20 * k)), none for an empty file. Trebago is
! exact and has no floor, so the ceiling is counted: ceil(v / d) is
! floor(x / d) with x = v + d - 1, and floor(x / d) is found three
! decimal digits at a time, each digit the count of j = 1 to 999 with
! j * step * d <= x, which min(1, max(0, x - j * step * d + 1)) is for
! integers; what each digit takes is subtracted before the next. Four
! digits of three hold every answer here (below 10^11). ok is 1 for a
! size 0..999999999999 and k 1..168 (freight.pack's rows), else 0, and the
! answer is divided by it: anything else is a division by zero, refused,
! where freights.kron answers: held.
trebago freight_count
  in  size(n), k(n)
  out freights(n)
  var x(n), dv(n), ok(n), a(n), b(n), c(n), d(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, size(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 999999999999 - size(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, k(i))) * min(1, max(0, 168 - k(i) + 1))
  dv(i) = 20 * k(i)
  x(i) = size(i) + dv(i) - 1
  a(i) = sum(j = 1:999, min(1, max(0, x(i) - j * 1000000000 * dv(i) + 1)))
  x(i) = x(i) - a(i) * 1000000000 * dv(i)
  b(i) = sum(j = 1:999, min(1, max(0, x(i) - j * 1000000 * dv(i) + 1)))
  x(i) = x(i) - b(i) * 1000000 * dv(i)
  c(i) = sum(j = 1:999, min(1, max(0, x(i) - j * 1000 * dv(i) + 1)))
  x(i) = x(i) - c(i) * 1000 * dv(i)
  d(i) = sum(j = 1:999, min(1, max(0, x(i) - j * dv(i) + 1)))
  freights(i) = (1000000000 * a(i) + 1000000 * b(i) + 1000 * c(i) + d(i)) / ok(i)
end
